<mxCell id="n19" value="Viewers" style="sketch=0;outlineConnect=0;fontColor=#232F3E;gradientColor=none;fillColor=#232F3D;strokeColor=none;dashed=0;html=1;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;aspect=fixed;pointerEvents=1;shape=mxgraph.aws4.user;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;verticalAlign=top;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="g4"><mxGeometry x="380" y="240" width="80" height="80" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="x20" value="1  Users call the public API.&lt;br&gt;2  The API writes each request to the raw-data bucket.&lt;br&gt;3  The collector reads new raw objects every hour (cross-account read).&lt;br&gt;4  The collector writes the cleaned copy to the curated bucket.&lt;br&gt;5  Athena reads the curated data through the Glue tables.&lt;br&gt;6  SPICE refreshes the datasets every day at 04:00 UTC.&lt;br&gt;7  The dashboard reads the SPICE datasets.&lt;br&gt;8  Viewers open the dashboard.&lt;br&gt;9  The identity-sync Lambda assumes the read-only role (ExternalId).&lt;br&gt;10  The role reads users and groups from IAM Identity Center.&lt;br&gt;11  User names are written to the identity-map bucket.&lt;br&gt;12  Athena joins the identity map to the curated data.&lt;br&gt;Dashed line: the central account reads the source account (pull).&lt;br&gt;Ingestion stack and Sync stack: one deployment each per source account." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=10;fontColor=#545B64;fontStyle=1;whiteSpace=nowrap;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="750" width="412" height="182" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
